## LAB 6 — Microsoft Entra Connect (Identity Sync)

### Step-by-step
1. Create a **Microsoft 365 Developer tenant** or Entra ID free tier if you don't already have a tenant — gives you `yourtenant.onmicrosoft.com`.
2. Install **Microsoft Entra Connect** (formerly Azure AD Connect) on a **member server** (not the DC — best practice), or the DC itself if lab resources are constrained.
3. Choose sync method during setup — for lab purposes, pick **Password Hash Synchronization (PHS)**: simplest, most common in real deployments, no extra infrastructure needed (Pass-through Auth needs connector agents; Federation needs ADFS — save those for later exploration).
4. During setup, select which OUs to sync — sync only `OU_HQ` (not built-in containers) to keep it clean.
5. Enable **Password Writeback** if you want password changes in the cloud to sync back on-prem (optional but good to practice).
6. Run initial sync, then verify in **Entra Admin Center (entra.microsoft.com) > Users** — your on-prem users should now appear as "synced from on-premises directory."
7. Check sync health: **Microsoft Entra Connect Health** or just re-run `Start-ADSyncSyncCycle -PolicyType Delta` after making an AD change, and confirm it reflects in the cloud within minutes.

### Checklist
- [ ] Entra Connect installed and initial sync completed
- [ ] On-prem users visible in Entra Admin Center
- [ ] Delta sync tested (change an attribute on-prem, confirm it syncs)

