## LAB 7 — Entra Users, MFA, Roles

### Step-by-step
1. In **Entra Admin Center**, create a couple of **cloud-only** users (not synced) to understand the difference vs. synced identities.
2. Enable **Security Defaults** (free, simplest MFA enforcement) if you don't have Entra ID P1/P2 — Entra Admin Center > Properties > Manage Security Defaults > On.
   - If you have P1 trial: build a real **Conditional Access policy** instead (e.g. "Require MFA for all users" — much closer to real enterprise practice).
3. Have a test user register for MFA: sign in at `myaccount.microsoft.com`, add Authenticator app method.
4. **Assign Entra roles** (RBAC) — practice with built-in roles:
   - Assign a user as **User Administrator** (can reset passwords, manage users) — NOT Global Admin, to practice least-privilege.
   - Assign another as **Helpdesk Administrator**.
5. Document the difference between **on-prem AD groups** (Lab 2) and **Entra roles** (this lab) — different purposes: AD groups = resource access, Entra roles = admin permissions over the tenant itself.

### Checklist
- [ ] MFA enforced (Security Defaults or Conditional Access) and tested with a real sign-in
- [ ] At least 2 different Entra roles assigned to different test users
- [ ] Clear understanding documented of AD groups vs. Entra roles distinction

