## LAB 9 — File Server → SharePoint Migration

### Step-by-step
1. In Microsoft 365 Admin Center, create a **SharePoint site** per department (or one site with document libraries per team — decide based on your OU structure from Lab 2).
2. Install **SharePoint Migration Tool (SPMT)** on a machine with access to your on-prem file shares.
3. **Before migrating** — audit your NTFS permissions structure (Lab 2 groups) and manually map them to SharePoint permission levels; they don't translate automatically.
4. Run a **test migration** of one small folder first (e.g. `Public`), verify:
   - Files/folders intact
   - Permissions correctly applied to the equivalent SharePoint group
   - No broken links or unsupported characters (SharePoint has stricter filename rules — `#`, `%`, trailing spaces will error)
5. Migrate remaining shares one department at a time, not all at once.
6. Set up **OneDrive sync** on the client VM so users can access the migrated library like a mapped drive.
7. Document lessons learned: what broke, what needed manual permission remapping.

### Checklist
- [ ] SharePoint site(s) created matching org structure
- [ ] Test migration completed and verified
- [ ] Full migration completed with permissions manually validated (not just copied blindly)
- [ ] Client VM can access migrated content via OneDrive sync

