## LAB 10 — Exchange Online

### Step-by-step
1. In Microsoft 365 Admin Center, assign **Exchange Online licenses** to your synced users (from Lab 6).
2. Verify **mailboxes provision automatically** for synced users (can take a few minutes to a few hours).
3. If practicing a "real" migration scenario, set up **Hybrid Configuration Wizard** (only if you also install an on-prem Exchange Server — optional, heavier lab; many home labs skip full hybrid Exchange and just do a clean cloud mailbox setup instead).
4. Configure basic **mail flow rules** in Exchange Admin Center (e.g., disclaimer footer, internal-only distribution list).
5. Create a **Distribution List** and a **Shared Mailbox** tied to your OU/department structure.
6. Test send/receive between two lab users via Outlook Web Access (OWA).

### Checklist
- [ ] Licenses assigned, mailboxes provisioned
- [ ] At least one mail flow rule configured
- [ ] Distribution list and shared mailbox created
- [ ] Successful test email between two users

