## LAB 12 — Microsoft Defender (Security)

### Step-by-step
1. Enable **Microsoft Defender for Endpoint** on the client VM and Azure VM(s) — onboard via Intune (Lab 11) configuration profile or manual onboarding script.
2. In **Microsoft 365 Defender portal**, verify devices appear and are reporting.
3. Enable **Microsoft Defender for Identity** (monitors your on-prem AD/DC for suspicious activity) — install the sensor on your DC.
4. Configure a basic **Attack Simulation** (Defender portal > Email & Collaboration > Attack simulation training) to test phishing awareness against a test user.
5. Review the **Secure Score** dashboard — this ties together everything from Labs 6-12 into a single security posture metric.
6. Set up at least one **alert policy** (e.g. impossible travel sign-in, multiple failed logins) and trigger it artificially to confirm alerting works end-to-end.

### Checklist
- [ ] Devices onboarded and reporting into Defender portal
- [ ] Defender for Identity sensor active on DC
- [ ] At least one alert policy tested and confirmed working
- [ ] Secure Score reviewed and understood

